cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the
  article that the sampler follows.
type: software
title: "bsfa: Bayesian Stochastic Frontier Analysis"
abstract: >-
  Bayesian inference for stochastic frontier models by Markov chain Monte
  Carlo. Gibbs samplers with data augmentation are provided for
  composed-error frontier models in the tradition of van den Broeck, Koop,
  Osiewalski and Steel (1994), covering exponential and half-normal
  inefficiency, production and cost frontiers, and cross-sectional,
  time-invariant panel and four-component panel specifications. Because the
  one-sided inefficiency term is sampled as a latent variable rather than
  integrated out, posterior distributions of unit-specific efficiency scores
  are obtained directly from the augmented draws rather than from point
  predictors.
